From 91a779fa1aa18d9496b9bc18690f1b642f113cd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:18:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/32] fix(qwen4_exp): load ModelOpt MIXED_PRECISION QAD
 checkpoints

ModelOpt serializes an MXFP8 linear as weight (e4m3) + weight_scale (uint8
E8M0, one per 32 inputs); Fp8LinearMethod(use_mxfp8) names that parameter
weight_scale_inv. The scale fell into the skipped-_scale branch and hit the
1.0 assert (C3 boot, layers.0.mlp.shared_expert.down_proj). Rename uint8
.weight_scale -> .weight_scale_inv and raise if any renamed scale finds no
parameter, instead of silently dropping it.

The Qwen3-VL vision tower is always built unquantized, but this checkpoint
ships it MXFP8 + W4A16_NVFP4 (linear_fc2). Dequantize those groups to bf16
at load (exact w.r.t. the checkpoint values; same footprint as a bf16-vision
checkpoint). Conventions checked against RadixArk bf16 tensors of the same
base model: E8M0 bias 127, NVFP4 low nibble first.

test/manual/qwen4_exp_qad_load_dryrun.py: CPU-only meta-device walk of
load_weights (target + NEXTN draft) over every checkpoint tensor; asserts
each tensor consumed once, every parameter written, no dtype-changing write.
